virtio_console: a read takes every buffer that is there

A port's receive buffers are PAGE_SIZE each and a read(2) returned at most one, so the host's
large messages (the decoded pictures of a webos.media DECODE session) took a system call
per 4 KB: about 450 per 1280x720 picture, which on a TCG guest cost more than half a second.
A read now copies from every filled buffer while there is room, as a pipe read does.

--- a/drivers/char/virtio_console.c
+++ b/drivers/char/virtio_console.c
@@ -770,7 +770,18 @@
 	if (!port_has_data(port) && !port->host_connected)
 		return 0;
 
-	return fill_readbuf(port, ubuf, count, true);
+	/* As much as is there, not one PAGE_SIZE buffer per call. */
+	ret = 0;
+	do {
+		ssize_t n = fill_readbuf(port, ubuf + ret, count - ret, true);
+
+		if (n < 0)
+			return ret ? ret : n;
+		if (!n)
+			break;
+		ret += n;
+	} while (ret < count && port_has_data(port));
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int wait_port_writable(struct port *port, bool nonblock)
